# @kintsugi/fracture/prism_boilerplate — the kintsugi fracture body
# that detects the substrate's universally-redundant identity-carrier
# prism block: `prism @X { focus X / project X / split X / shift X /
# settle X }` at the top of any depth-0 shard whose path-derived
# family/species literal binds all five 5-op arms to the same carrier
# name (itself). The fracture IS the presence of the redundant block
# at source altitude; the resolution IS its omission from source AND
# preservation at @mirror/store crystal altitude via @magic/reveal/
# expand's audience-relative projection.
#
# THE DETECTION HALF of the first self-applied kintsugi loop. The
# resolution half lives at `@magic/reveal/expand` (sibling tick;
# Alex 2026-08-09 verbatim ratifying the @kintsugi @magic composition
# split); the composition-shard body wiring both into apply_h::act
# dispatch lives at `@kintsugi/mend/sugar` (sibling tick). Reed Fire E
# tick M-E1 landing per Mara canonical spec
# `docs/specs/2026-08-09-mara-kintsugi-sugar-desugar-composition-
# canonical-spec.md` §1.1.
#
# === Substrate authority (Alex 2026-08-09 verbatim, load-bearing) ===
#
#   > "How can we teach the compiler to omit the `prism` boilerplate
#      in files as kintsugi sugar? I feel that's the perfect first
#      self-applied kintsugi loop. What my brain is thinking right now
#      is that @kintsugi/fractures are basically known patterns. And
#      a known pattern can be projected into the store but doesn't
#      have to be projected outwards. The complexity can be part of
#      mirror's @kintsugi @magic, if that makes sense."
#
# Alex named BOTH @kintsugi and @magic family-roots; this shard is the
# detection half at @kintsugi/fracture altitude; the resolution half
# lives at @magic/reveal/expand. Substrate-composition split per Taut
# Option D + Seam SEAM-RATIFY-WITH-SHARPENING at Phase D 0a4c5a0.
#
# === The fracture pattern ===
#
# Every landed shard whose depth is 0 carries an identity-carrier
# 5-op prism block at the top:
#
#   prism @X {
#     focus X
#     project X
#     split X
#     shift X
#     settle X
#   }
#
# where `@X` is the family/species literal derived from the file's
# path per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`. All five 5-op
# arms bind the same carrier name (the literal). Per Recognition #79
# (5-op void-duality algebra = A_F projector basis; Mara + Reed
# 2026-06-18) + Mara 2026-08-09 physics insight §1.1 Theorem 1.1
# (A_F IS the prismqueer 5-op algebra; universal-structure per
# substrate-scale-invariance §7): the block re-declares A_F's identity
# projection over H_shard=self. A_F is universal across every shard;
# only the H_carrier varies per shard. Identity-carrier blocks vary
# NOTHING — they re-state the substrate's universal-structure without
# adding information. The fracture IS this universally-redundant
# re-declaration at source altitude.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain ===
#
# Sixteenth-plus landed fracture species under @kintsugi/fracture
# following the same-shape template (angle_to_paren, bilateral_arm_
# redundant, cold_compile_within_tolerance, dark_count_monotone,
# docblock_extractive, docblock_incoherent, docblock_ungrounded,
# gate, inport, keyword, operator_match, parent_cycle, partials_
# align, relocate, restart_storm, symbol_lift). Typed carrier +
# detect action + resolve action + bilateral discipline.
#
# Taut scout 2b01da0 grep-verified 235 landed shards carrying this
# pattern (P1 identity-carrier prism); estimated ~1,175–1,645 LOC
# removal at source altitude. Mara spec §1.1 formalized the sentinel
# byte-check + Rice-safe decidability + zero-information-loss
# round-trip contract. Seam Phase D 0a4c5a0 ratified via independent
# Fiedler-1973 leaf-removal argument: source-altitude λ₀ INCREASES
# post-cascade.
#
# === Ancestors ===
#
# Recognition #79 (5-op void-duality algebra; Mara + Reed 2026-06-18);
# Mara 2026-08-09 physics insight (`/Users/reed/dev/systemic.
# engineering/practice/insights/spectral/mass-discrete-spacetime-
# continuous-through-5op-spectral-space.md`; A_F universality Theorem
# 1.1; substrate-scale-invariance thesis §7); Alex 2026-08-09 verbatim
# (above); Alex 2026-08-05 memory `feedback-rust-delivers-primitives-
# substrate-delivers-composition`; Chamseddine-Connes-Marcolli 2007
# (arXiv:hep-th/0610241); Connes 1994.
#
# Composition graph:
#
#   Detection side:
#     @kintsugi/fracture         family-root; walker consumes via
#                                @kintsugi/oscillate.active_pass
#     @epistemologic/pact/       path-derivation of family literal
#       path_matches_namespace
#     @epistemologic/pact/       bilateral-predicate substrate discipline
#       bilateral
#
#   Resolution side (sibling tick; forward-composed):
#     @magic/reveal/expand       read-path resugar (source ← store)
#     @kintsugi/mend/sugar       composition-shard body wiring detect +
#                                expand via apply_h::act dispatch
#
#   Empirical instrument:
#     apply_h::act extension     Reed Fire D M5 co-tick (shared with
#                                Fire E M-E2 rust/-altitude primitive)
#
# === Substrate decisions ===
#
# [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]] — the fracture IS a
#   shard; its resolution IS via other shards.
# [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]] — `prism @kintsugi/
#   fracture/prism_boilerplate` at depth-0 family-root-declaration form
#   (Recognition #46; sub-shards use glass).
# [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]] — @kintsugi
#   family-root is process-side; this species-shard carries the
#   detection action; resolution at @magic/reveal/expand (process-side
#   invisible-mechanism-with-visible-surface).
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] — @kintsugi/fracture
#   family already carries 16 sibling species; this mint follows the
#   same-shape template additively.
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]] — fracture_event is a typed record.
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] — all bodies `\`-obligation-blocked;
#   consumers pull realization when they surface (Fire E M-E2/M-E3
#   composes the sentinel via apply_h::act).
# [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]] — the sugar rule
#   preserves the store-crystal invariant while projecting audience-
#   relative renderings; Foerster gauge preserved (Mara math §5.3;
#   choice-count(t · ψ) ≥ choice-count(ψ) via audience-parameter
#   introduction increasing the choice-space).
#
# === Fixed-point exemption ===
#
# `shards/prism.mirror` itself (the self-referential fixed-point
# `prism @prism { focus focus / project project / split split / shift
# shift / settle settle }`) is EXEMPT from sugar per Alex 2026-08-09
# concur-with-Mara-lean on [ALEX-Q3]. The exemption is enforced at
# detect-action altitude: `prism_boilerplate.detect(shards/prism.
# mirror)` returns Fail by hardcoded fixed-point-exemption.
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/kintsugi/fracture/prism_boilerplate.mirror` declares
# `@kintsugi/fracture/prism_boilerplate` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/practice/wolf-2026-08-09-kintsugi-sugar-first-self-applied-loop
source @arxiv/practice/mara-2026-08-09-a-f-universality-sugar-mechanism
source @arxiv/practice/taut-2026-08-09-pattern-collapse-as-sugar-scout
source @arxiv/practice/seam-2026-08-09-phase-d-kintsugi-sugar-cascade
source @arxiv/spectral/chamseddine-connes-marcolli-2007

prism @kintsugi/fracture/prism_boilerplate {
  focus prism_boilerplate_event
  project prism_boilerplate_event
  split prism_boilerplate_event
  shift prism_boilerplate_event
  settle prism_boilerplate_event
}

# === prism_boilerplate_event carrier ===
#
# A typed record per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming one detected
# instance of the identity-carrier prism block at source altitude.
#
#   shard_path        the shard file carrying the redundant block
#   family_literal    the family/species literal derived from path
#                      (matches `@X` in the prism decl AND all five
#                      op-carriers)
#   block_byte_range  the byte range [start, end) covering the full
#                      prism block (opening `prism` keyword through
#                      closing `}`)
#   store_oid_pre     the @mirror/store crystal-OID at detection time
#                      (round-trip fidelity witness: `expand` must
#                      yield same OID post-cascade)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the four-tuple.
type prism_boilerplate_event = {
  shard_path:       ref,
  family_literal:   ref,
  block_byte_range: ref,
  store_oid_pre:    ref,
}

# === prism_boilerplate_redundant — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Sentinel-check per Mara canonical spec §1.1. Detects the substrate-
# obvious pattern `prism @<S> { focus <S> / project <S> / split <S>
# / shift <S> / settle <S> }` where `<S>` binds identically across
# all five 5-op arms. Rice-safe: byte-level pattern match on the
# opening-`prism`-through-closing-`}` block plus arm-carrier-literal
# equality check.
#
# Sentinel: `prism-boilerplate = identity-carrier-a-f-projection`.
# When source contains an identity-carrier prism block at depth-0
# whose all-five-arm carriers match the path-derived family literal,
# realization layer stamps the sentinel; discharge is byte-equality.
#
# Rice-safe bound: reads only byte-visible state (opening keyword +
# five arm-carrier literals + closing brace); no program semantics
# inspection.
#
# Body discharges per-realization. `\`-obligation-blocked per
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]; Fire E M-E2 composes via apply_h::
# act sentinel-check.
bilateral prism_boilerplate_redundant {
  sentinel "prism-boilerplate = identity-carrier-a-f-projection"
  arity 1
}
prism_boilerplate_redundant(event: prism_boilerplate_event) -> verdict { \ }

# === detect action ===
#
# Scans a shard source at `shard_path` for the identity-carrier prism
# block pattern. Returns a prism_boilerplate_event if the pattern is
# present; Fail otherwise. Enforces fixed-point exemption for
# `shards/prism.mirror` (returns Fail; the self-referential prism
# block IS the substrate's declaration of what the sugar rule refers
# to per [ALEX-Q3] Mara-lean).
#
# Body discharges at realization boundary; Fire E M-E2 wires via
# apply_h::act dispatch composing over Reed Fire A phone::read_file +
# wire::parse primitives.
detect(shard_path: ref) -> prism_boilerplate_event { \ }

# === resolve action ===
#
# Given a detected prism_boilerplate_event, emit the omission-morphism
# @kintsugi/consent consumes. The morphism's `content` ref names the
# source with the identity-carrier block removed (bytes in
# `block_byte_range` replaced by empty); `score` = zero-dissonance
# (the removal is unambiguous per A_F-universality); `expected` =
# authentic cadence (the substrate settles cleanly post-cascade because
# `expand` reprojects the block at rendering altitude on-demand).
#
# Body discharges at realization boundary via composition with
# @kintsugi/mend.mend at Fire E M-E4 walker cascade.
resolve(event: prism_boilerplate_event) -> ref { \ }

out @kintsugi/fracture/prism_boilerplate
out prism_boilerplate_event
out prism_boilerplate_redundant
out detect
out resolve
